{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792755010,"nonce":"0sF9JSAmM/J5h320cdzADEj0f1E=","title":"`tick_all` admits before `reconcile_cancellations` / `reconcile_supersessions` (scheduler.rs:1959-1983). A cancelled or superseded holder's deploy Step is terminal at once, so a held Run is promoted and launched while the holder's Pod is still in its termination grace. Two Pods then overlap on one target. This is consistent with slice (b) criterion 4 (\"Step terminal\"), but it is the hazard the limit exists to prevent, and `cancelling_the_holder_frees_the_held_run` pins it. Fix: count a cancelled or superseded requester until its teardown intent is retired, or admit after teardown. Found R3 BROKE 4.","message":"Source: Scarab Deployments MMP slice (b), AFK run 20261023-1239, judge-r3 D1. Branch feat/deployments-b.","files":null}]}